   "created_at": "2026-10-25T17:36:40Z",
   "updated_at": "2026-10-25T17:36:40Z",
   "body": "The check that lets a tool-output hash through read only the span's first field: the model takes `1 2f1d0c9b…a291` as one span, the first field is the count `1`, and `hexRe` wants 7 or more hex digits, so the span survived as a secret.\n\nFixed on [fix/redact-hex-count](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/redact-hex-count) (`50f6e8b5`, based on today's `main`): the hex-run exemption now reads every field of the span — a hex run with nothing but counts around it (`numberedHash`) is a hash in a tool's output, exactly as one with words after it already was.\n\n- Red → green: `TestModelMisreadsNotMasked` gained the model's span verbatim (`1 2f1d…`, as `testdata/eval-model.json` recorded it); the masking evaluation's `hex-lines` case now comes out right on the \"both\" column, and its `Known: \"#3597\"` marker is off.\n- Full `internal/redact` suite (`-tags nogui`): 82 passed, nothing else moved.\n\nNo real account or network was touched.\n",
